    "result": "I implemented `order_total` in `solution.py` following `spec.md`, and wrote 38 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py`. `python -m pytest -q tests` passes (38 passed).\n\nThe implementation validates items first, then checks the coupon (all failures raise `CouponError`), then computes the percent or capped fixed discount, adds shipping based on the discounted subtotal (free at 100.00 or more, none for an empty order), and rounds the total to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. I split it into small helpers so each function stays low in complexity. The tests cover the boundaries (expiry date, minimum subtotal, 0 and 100 percent, the 100.00 shipping threshold, and half-cent rounding) along with each error path. One test expectation I first wrote was wrong (a 0.5% coupon on 100.00 leaves 99.50, which is still under the threshold), and I corrected the test, not the code.\n\nI have not run the coverage, CRAP, mutation or bandit gates. Only the pytest command was run, since the shell is restricted to it.",
